WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:11.080
Luckily Floyd didn't go far.

2
00:00:11.081 --> 00:00:16.759
He ran into the pasture.

3
00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:19.444
"Whew!" Kaleem said.

4
00:00:19.445 --> 00:00:22.694
"He still sounds unhappy, but he's safe."

5
00:00:22.695 --> 00:00:29.043
"Jon, what happened?" Jan cried. "Why is Floyd so upset?"

6
00:00:29.044 --> 00:00:33.492
Jon shrugged. "I thought I'd try putting him with the donkeys.

7
00:00:33.493 --> 00:00:36.369
Then the dog scared him, I guess."

8
00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:39.499
"Sorry!" Daisy felt sheepish.

9
00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:43.531
She hadn't realized that a llama might be scared of a dog.

10
00:00:43.532 --> 00:00:48.082
"Don't blame yourself." Jon sighed.

11
00:00:48.083 --> 00:00:50.743
"We had trouble getting Floyd here too.

12
00:00:50.744 --> 00:00:53.876
The farm he came from is only a mile away.

13
00:00:53.877 --> 00:00:58.810
We thought it would be easy to walk him here. But he kept trying to turn back."

14
00:00:58.811 --> 00:01:02.775
The cow and horses were eying the llama curiously.

15
00:01:02.776 --> 00:01:06.040
"Oh, great," Floyd grumbled.

16
00:01:06.041 --> 00:01:09.119
"Like my life wasn't terrible enough!

17
00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:14.833
Now I have to share a pasture with silly horses and a smelly cow."

18
00:01:14.834 --> 00:01:18.753
"I beg your pardon!" The cow sounded offended.

19
00:01:18.754 --> 00:01:23.527
"We'd better call the llama farm and ask for help," Jan said.

20
00:01:23.528 --> 00:01:30.334
"Good idea," Jon said. "Let's go call them. My phone's in the barn."

21
00:01:30.335 --> 00:01:33.028
The adults hurried away.

22
00:01:33.029 --> 00:01:36.924
"Finn, please don't bark at Floyd," Daisy said.

23
00:01:36.925 --> 00:01:41.151
"I'm going to see if I can fix this."

24
00:01:41.152 --> 00:01:50.597
She gave Finn's leash to Kaleem and went to the fence.

25
00:01:50.598 --> 00:01:56.235
"Pardon me, Floyd. I'm Daisy. Why did you say your life is terrible?"

26
00:01:56.236 --> 00:02:01.790
Floyd looked surprised.

27
00:02:01.791 --> 00:02:06.298
"You understood me? How unusual.

28
00:02:06.299 --> 00:02:12.578
If my life wasn't falling apart, I might even find this conversation interesting."

29
00:02:12.579 --> 00:02:15.595
"This is a nice farm," Daisy said.

30
00:02:15.596 --> 00:02:18.758
"I think you can be happy here."

31
00:02:18.759 --> 00:02:22.672
Floyd sniffed. "No, I can't.

32
00:02:22.673 --> 00:02:25.686
Not without any other llamas around.

33
00:02:25.687 --> 00:02:28.980
We're herd animals, you know."

34
00:02:28.981 --> 00:02:35.519
"Oh. Actually I didn't know that." Once again Daisy felt sheepish.

35
00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:40.359
"What if I suggest that Jan and Jon get another llama from the llama farm?

36
00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:42.499
It could keep you company."

37
00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:46.307
"Really? You'd do that?" Floyd said.

38
00:02:46.308 --> 00:02:51.605
"Can you tell these owners that I'd like them to get Joker or Flower?

39
00:02:51.606 --> 00:02:59.176
I don't care for Maurice. He thinks he's so fancy with his spotted fur!"

40
00:02:59.177 --> 00:03:01.994
Jan and Jon returned.

41
00:03:01.995 --> 00:03:04.036
Jan was smiling.

42
00:03:04.037 --> 00:03:10.175
"The llama farmer says llamas are happier in a herd, or at least with some other llamas."

43
00:03:10.176 --> 00:03:14.145
Jon nodded. "We're going to get another llama right now.

44
00:03:14.146 --> 00:03:18.229
Sorry to cut your visit short, kids. Please come back again."

45
00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:20.035
Daisy was relieved.

46
00:03:20.036 --> 00:03:24.877
Now she wouldn't need to figure out how to tell the couple what Floyd had said.

47
00:03:24.878 --> 00:03:29.196
Just then Beatrice buzzed loudly from Daisy's headband.

48
00:03:29.197 --> 00:03:32.520
"You're forgetting something!"

49
00:03:32.521 --> 00:03:36.106
"Oh!" Daisy cleared her throat.

50
00:03:36.107 --> 00:03:39.022
"I, um, read this somewhere.

51
00:03:39.023 --> 00:03:43.949
Some llamas don't like other llamas with spots.

52
00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:46.792
Maybe you should get a solid-colored one."

53
00:03:46.793 --> 00:03:49.156
Jan and Jon looked surprised.

54
00:03:49.157 --> 00:03:51.997
Then Jan chuckled.

55
00:03:51.998 --> 00:03:57.069
"Whatever you say, Daisy. We're still learning about llamas."

56
00:03:57.070 --> 00:04:03.100
Jon nodded. "We'll take anyone's advice. A solid-colored llama it is!"

57
00:04:03.101 --> 00:04:05.795
"Splendid," Floyd said.

58
00:04:05.796 --> 00:04:11.363
"Thanks, Daisy. You're no llama or anything, but you're not bad for a human."

59
00:04:11.364 --> 00:04:18.319
Daisy giggled. It was probably the best compliment she'd ever had.

60
00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:21.348
"What's so funny?" Kaleem asked.

61
00:04:21.349 --> 00:04:24.287
"I'll tell you later," Daisy said.

62
00:04:24.288 --> 00:04:30.883
"Let's take Detective Finn home!"

